          <attvalue for="36" value="A sustained rise in long-term sovereign yields increases debt-service burdens and refinancing costs for governments, forcing fiscal retrenchment (cuts to subsidies, investment or transfers) that erodes the governing party's capacity to implement major energy and foreign-policy decisions." />
